{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Window Event Queue.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Window Event Queue.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender window event queue blender window event queue","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Window Event Queue.md","fileName":"Blender Window Event Queue.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Window Event Queue","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Operator and Event System]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Operator and Event System","Blender Window Structure","Blender GHOST Event Translation","Blender Window Event Processing","Blender Region Event Routing","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Window Event Queue.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Window Event Queue.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender window event queue blender window event queue","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Window Event Queue.md","fileName":"Blender Window Event Queue.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Window Event Queue","heading":"Blender Window Event Queue","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Each [[Blender Window Structure]] maintains a queue of Blender event records awaiting dispatch. [[Blender GHOST Event Translation]] copies native input into the application's event representation and appends it to the active window instead of immediately guessing which editor should handle it.\n\nSeparating capture from dispatch lets [[Blender Window Event Processing]] traverse events with the current screen, scene, and view-layer context in place. Each event can then proceed through [[Blender Region Event Routing]] and its installed handler list in a controlled order.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender O